edge.test.ts is the instrument, checked in, asserting bounds rather than
equalities so a tighter edge can never fail the suite. Reverting to the pure
cell decision fails 7 of its assertions; narrowing the band to one ring
fails the same 7.

A fixture for the object-protection invariant was drafted and DELETED rather
than shipped, and the file says so: it could not be made to fail. A
synthetic object in wood's own hue is either far enough from the floor's
brightness that every version protects it or close enough that every version
paints it — measured at four brightness levels, the transition is a step
with no window between. AUDIT-01 is the real guard for that property and is
provably sensitive to it.

All ten floor-studio suites pass: 65,216 assertions. 65 of 66 guards pass;
verify:css cannot run in this sandbox (postcss unresolvable, npm 403) and
fails identically on a clean checkout. parse-scan clean. Typecheck clean.

